    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d500">

                <pb facs="0565" n="549" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg549"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.51/11–2547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in Chile
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-25T11:00:00-05:00">November 25,
                            1947—11 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>563. For Emb
                    info only. Robert Vergara informed Dept that on
                    Nov 18 he had reached agreement with Rogers, Pres, For Bondholders Protective Council, on terms settlement of
                        Chil debt which provide initial interest
                    1–½ percent rising to 3 percent after 1953 and 1 percent amortization.
                    Announcement agreement probably be delayed few weeks since related negotiations
                    with British and Swiss bondholders groups not concluded.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
